---
import:
  - stdlib/lang/go
  - stdlib/cli/common
description: A command-line tool in Go 1.25 with Cobra.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: uses Cobra, with `main` in `cmd/<tool>/`, one file per command in `internal/cli/`, the work in packages under `internal/`, and the tool's errors under `internal/errs`.
  - Every command uses `RunE`, and the root command sets `SilenceUsage` and `SilenceErrors`, so `main` alone writes the error and chooses the exit code.
  - It builds with `go build -o bin/<tool> ./cmd/<tool>`.
- :Implementation: logs with a `slog.TextHandler` on standard error, at the level `--verbose` or `--debug` gives.
- :UnitTests: run commands through the root command with `SetArgs`, `SetOut` and `SetErr`.
